From 9e50cac9e1849dd6fdce8349f3f3bd1be4325fa6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:30:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fused K / V cache write for a q4_0 KV cache too

The rope + FWHT kernels that write the rotated K row (and the V row) straight into the KV cache
(rms_norm_mul_rope_f32 kv, the Q / K pair, the rope-only form) quantized only to q8_0, so a q4_0 cache kept
its separate SET_ROWS launches, V's fwht_cuda and the single Q / K launches.  ggml_cuda_quantize_q4_0_group
quantizes a 32-lane group exactly as quantize_f32_q4_0_block does (the scan's first element of largest |v|,
never a NaN, +0 for an all-zero group; the same rounding), and the kernels take the cache type as a template
value (kv: 1 = q8_0, 2 = q4_0), so the q8_0 instantiations are unchanged.  wave32 only; V folds only into a K
write of its own type.  GGML_CUDA_KV_FOLD_Q4_0=0: q8_0 only.
